# Editing a file
> `nano` is a small editor: type to insert, Ctrl-O saves, Ctrl-X leaves. UP-Term's startup
> file for your own aliases and settings is $HOME/.vshrc (HOME is SYS: unless you
> changed it); vsh reads it every time it starts.
? Make the file mynotes.txt with one line in it, using echo and >.
= [ -s mynotes.txt ]
~ echo hello > mynotes.txt
! echo hello > mynotes.txt
? Open mynotes.txt in nano, change the text, save with Ctrl-O and leave with Ctrl-X.
= [ -f mynotes.txt ] && case "$LEARN_LINE" in "nano mynotes.txt") true ;; *) false ;; esac
~ nano mynotes.txt
! nano mynotes.txt
? Show the file again to see your change.
= grep -q . "$LEARN_OUT"
~ cat mynotes.txt
! cat mynotes.txt
